[block
  'ORD-0011-case-stores'
  [ctx
    'the spec of EMS-002'
    '.guidelines/.orders/EMS-002/EMS-002.pgml'
  [/ctx]
  [tgt
    'the snapshot honours the stores of each case, O5 of INTAKE-RUST-LADDER, answered on 2026-09-27'
  [/tgt]
  [ctx
    'the snapshot and the oracle project every declared case with one uniform set of stores, the repository ones, so a case that brings its own templates is projected without them, and TemplateCycle, whose cases bring a cyclic store, never reaches the oracle'
  [/ctx]
  [cnst
    'a case is projected with its stores laid over the repository ones, the reading the decision names: measured before the code, it moves exactly T-07, T-08 and T-09, the two cycles among them; the case stores alone would move 36 cases, the C and K cases with them'
  [/cnst]
  [cnst
    'the snapshot moves by decision, and the decision is written; a hash that moves outside the T cases is a regression, not the decision'
  [/cnst]
  [cmp
    'the snapshot'
    'each declared case is projected with its own stores laid over the repository ones, the T hashes move by decision, and no other hash moves'
    [ctx[/ctx]
    [cnst[/cnst]
  [/cmp]
  [sub
    [eq
      [cmp
        [ctx[/ctx]
      [/cmp]
    [/eq]
  [/sub]
  [elab
    [eq[/eq]
    [sub[/sub]
    [rsn[/rsn]
  [/elab]
  [ref
    [cnst[/cnst]
  [/ref]
  [ctx[/ctx]
  [core[/core]
  [core[/core]
  [elab[/elab]
  [cmp
    'the oracle'
    'TemplateCycle enters the oracle, the case files and the runs say which stores a case brings, and the Rust answers them byte for byte'
    [ctx[/ctx]
    [cnst[/cnst]
  [/cmp]
